THUG2 decompilation - licensing

This repository contains two kinds of material.

1. Reconstructed game code (no licence granted)

   The C++ under src/game that reconstructs Tony Hawk's Underground 2 (PC) - every function registered with a REPLACE /
   REPLACE_SOURCE_ONLY line against an address of the original executable - is a re-expression of a game whose
   copyright belongs to Activision Publishing, Inc. and its licensors. No licence of any kind is granted for it, and
   none could be: the authors of this repository do not own the rights to the game. It is published for preservation,
   interoperability and educational purposes only. See NOTICE.md.

2. Original work (MIT licence)

   Everything written for this project that is not a reconstruction of the original game is licensed under the MIT
   licence below. That includes the hook and test framework (src/hook, src/proxy), the self-tests, all code marked
   NOT ORIGINAL in src/game (for example the new front end, the level editor, the THAW BMX port, the graphics options
   and the screenshot, automation and mute tools), the tools (tools/ - the content pipeline and the Anteara Mod are
   separate repositories with their own MIT licence), the documentation (docs/) and the design files (docs/design).

   Third-party code and data used by the project keep their own licences: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

